1
00:00:02,002 --> 00:00:03,122
JIM: <i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:03,270 --> 00:00:06,399
My name is Volk. My brother, Jacob.
We are called "the Whisper Gang."

3
00:00:06,573 --> 00:00:08,017
BRUCE: <i>Those men were
willing to kill for this key.</i>

4
00:00:08,041 --> 00:00:09,361
<i>- But what does it open?</i>
- A safe.

5
00:00:09,510 --> 00:00:12,446
Inside, there is a device that
we believe can destroy them.

6
00:00:12,613 --> 00:00:15,344
They call themselves
"The Court of Owls."

7
00:00:15,516 --> 00:00:17,576
Isabella was murdered.
Her brake lines were cut!

8
00:00:17,751 --> 00:00:18,751
<i>And I know who did it.</i>

9
00:00:18,919 --> 00:00:21,718
<i>You can stop the blade from being
released, if you click this button.</i>

10
00:00:21,889 --> 00:00:24,825
It will send a
fatal jolt to Butch.

11
00:00:24,992 --> 00:00:26,255
Hey, Butch? You're sweet.

12
00:00:26,793 --> 00:00:28,022
No!

13
00:00:28,195 --> 00:00:29,925
- You really didn't kill her?
- No!

14
00:00:30,097 --> 00:00:31,121
Guilty!

15
00:00:31,298 --> 00:00:34,268
The lab analyzing Alice Tetch's
blood has developed a test.

16
00:00:34,434 --> 00:00:35,434
You're kidding.

17
00:00:35,602 --> 00:00:38,128
Don Falcone, please,
we'll pull your car around.

18
00:00:40,073 --> 00:00:41,993
JIM: Carmine's not the
target. You are. Get down!

19
00:00:45,145 --> 00:00:46,841
Why are you coming after me?

20
00:00:47,014 --> 00:00:48,243
(CHOKING) You know why.

21
00:00:48,415 --> 00:00:49,883
Why are you
trying to kill my son?

22
00:00:50,050 --> 00:00:52,713
We will expect your
assistance when called on.

23
00:00:52,886 --> 00:00:54,718
Until then, your son is safe.

24
00:00:54,888 --> 00:00:56,288
At least from us.

25
00:00:57,124 --> 00:00:58,835
<i>Why does it feel like we
keep saying goodbye?</i>

26
00:00:58,859 --> 00:00:59,979
Maybe it's all we have left.

27
00:01:00,093 --> 00:01:02,562
Or we just haven't
done it properly yet.

28
00:01:02,729 --> 00:01:04,027
<i>Goodbye, James Gordon.</i>

29
00:01:04,197 --> 00:01:06,860
MARIO: <i>She loves
him. She loves him.</i>

30
00:01:07,034 --> 00:01:08,297
You lost?

31
00:01:09,336 --> 00:01:12,738
She loves <i>me!</i>

32
00:01:28,121 --> 00:01:29,121
Hey.

33
00:01:29,423 --> 00:01:30,423
(BEEPS)

34
00:01:34,328 --> 00:01:35,328
(DOOR OPENS)

35
00:01:35,862 --> 00:01:37,194
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

36
00:01:48,842 --> 00:01:50,333
I'm getting married tomorrow.

37
00:01:50,510 --> 00:01:52,240
Congratulations.

38
00:01:52,412 --> 00:01:54,904
You know, people always
talk about love at first sight.

39
00:01:55,816 --> 00:01:56,816
I never believed it.

40
00:01:56,984 --> 00:02:00,682
But the moment
I saw her, I knew.

41
00:02:01,121 --> 00:02:02,180
Yeah.

42
00:02:02,356 --> 00:02:04,120
So what do you do?

43
00:02:05,626 --> 00:02:08,255
I'm a hematologist
at Gotham Bio-Lab.

44
00:02:09,429 --> 00:02:12,263
You aren't working on
that blood virus, are you?

45
00:02:12,432 --> 00:02:16,961
From... What's her
name? Tetch? Alice Tetch?

46
00:02:18,238 --> 00:02:21,470
Uh, my fiancée is with
the police department.

47
00:02:21,642 --> 00:02:24,009
- She's the medical examiner on the case.
- Oh.

48
00:02:24,945 --> 00:02:26,140
Yes.

49
00:02:26,313 --> 00:02:29,181
She said you had come
up with a test for the virus.

50
00:02:29,816 --> 00:02:32,047
I really can't talk about it.

51
00:02:35,355 --> 00:02:37,915
She almost married someone else.

52
00:02:38,925 --> 00:02:43,124
I think her ex still hopes
she'll come running back.

53
00:02:43,964 --> 00:02:45,592
Not gonna happen.

54
00:02:49,503 --> 00:02:50,994
- Ah! (GRUNTS)
- (GLASS SHATTERS)

55
00:02:51,605 --> 00:02:55,007
MARIO: <i>She loves
him. She loves him.</i>

56
00:02:55,175 --> 00:02:56,336
<i>She loves him.</i>

57
00:02:56,510 --> 00:02:57,603
You hear me, Jim?

58
00:02:58,078 --> 00:03:00,912
I won't let you have her.

59
00:03:01,114 --> 00:03:02,480
- (SCREAMING)
- (SKULL CRACKLING)

60
00:03:02,649 --> 00:03:03,742
(SQUELCHING)

61
00:03:06,253 --> 00:03:07,448
(LAUGHING)

62
00:03:07,988 --> 00:03:10,014
(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)

63
00:03:17,164 --> 00:03:18,188
Volk is dead?

64
00:03:18,365 --> 00:03:21,267
We found his and Dmitry's
bodies early this morning.

65
00:03:21,435 --> 00:03:23,427
They were killed by
Talon, the Court's assassin.

66
00:03:23,603 --> 00:03:25,595
I'll say that changes
things a bit, doesn't it?

67
00:03:25,772 --> 00:03:28,742
How? You possess a
key. The key opens a safe.

68
00:03:29,176 --> 00:03:31,816
Inside the safe is an object that
can bring down the Court of Owls.

69
00:03:31,912 --> 00:03:33,107
None of these has changed.

70
00:03:37,984 --> 00:03:39,612
If this assassin
saw us with Volk...

71
00:03:39,786 --> 00:03:41,146
That means the
Court already knows

72
00:03:41,221 --> 00:03:43,122
that you're breaking
your deal, Master Bruce.

73
00:03:43,290 --> 00:03:44,485
I wish we knew for certain.

74
00:03:44,658 --> 00:03:47,492
Yeah, well, I wish we knew for
certain what was in that blinking safe

75
00:03:47,661 --> 00:03:50,654
or how far we can trust
this little Whisper Gang front.

76
00:03:50,831 --> 00:03:52,197
Now ask yourself this.

77
00:03:52,365 --> 00:03:56,166
Is bringing down the
Court really worth the risk?

78
00:04:02,109 --> 00:04:04,203
The Court of Owls has
taken over my company.

79
00:04:04,644 --> 00:04:06,078
Threatened people I care about,

80
00:04:06,246 --> 00:04:08,340
and is likely responsible
for my parents' deaths.

81
00:04:09,716 --> 00:04:11,446
What's our next step?

82
00:04:15,655 --> 00:04:18,318
- (INDISTINCT RADIO CHATTER)
- (CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING)

83
00:04:19,392 --> 00:04:20,826
I'm giving this one to Alvarez.

84
00:04:20,994 --> 00:04:21,994
No.

85
00:04:22,162 --> 00:04:23,562
<i>I told you to take the day off.</i>

86
00:04:24,064 --> 00:04:25,064
I know.

87
00:04:25,232 --> 00:04:27,098
You do know I'm acting
captain now, right?

88
00:04:27,267 --> 00:04:28,267
Yeah.

89
00:04:28,435 --> 00:04:30,267
Jim, there will be another
dead body tomorrow.

90
00:04:30,437 --> 00:04:32,804
Seriously, take the day.
Go fishing, get drunk.

91
00:04:32,973 --> 00:04:36,432
Harvey, this is my job. Lee
getting married doesn't change that.

92
00:04:36,610 --> 00:04:38,374
Take a look at this guy's head.

93
00:04:39,112 --> 00:04:41,274
Whoa, what's that
coming out of his ear?

94
00:04:41,448 --> 00:04:43,417
JIM: His skull was crushed.

95
00:04:43,583 --> 00:04:46,178
Like someone squeezed
it from either side.

96
00:04:46,353 --> 00:04:48,379
Can you imagine the
strength needed to do that?

97
00:04:48,822 --> 00:04:50,916
I gotta tell you,
my first thought.

98
00:04:51,091 --> 00:04:52,171
- (SCOFFS) Oh, no.
- Barnes.

99
00:04:52,259 --> 00:04:55,093
Stop it! Barnes had the
virus. He's at Arkham.

100
00:04:55,262 --> 00:04:57,288
That story's over. This
is what I was afraid of.

101
00:04:57,464 --> 00:05:00,628
Wallet's here, but the killer took a
badge or something from around his neck.

102
00:05:00,801 --> 00:05:02,099
Your emotions are all stirred.

103
00:05:02,269 --> 00:05:04,013
You're seeing things
that aren't really there.

104
00:05:04,037 --> 00:05:06,632
This is just a classic case
of wrong place, wrong time.

105
00:05:06,807 --> 00:05:09,572
One man takes another man's
skull in his bare hands and crushes it.

106
00:05:09,743 --> 00:05:11,143
I see it all the time.

107
00:05:11,311 --> 00:05:15,009
Receipt from the cafeteria
at Gotham Bio-Lab.

108
00:05:15,182 --> 00:05:17,276
Where Alice Tetch's
blood is being tested.

109
00:05:17,450 --> 00:05:18,509
Crap.

110
00:05:18,685 --> 00:05:20,483
I'm gonna swing by.
Finish up here, will you?

111
00:05:20,654 --> 00:05:23,590
Sure, Jim, happy to oblige.

112
00:05:25,992 --> 00:05:27,858
No rest for the wicked.

113
00:05:28,862 --> 00:05:29,862
Relax.

114
00:05:30,864 --> 00:05:34,426
I'm not here to get revenge
for you lopping off Tabby's paw.

115
00:05:34,601 --> 00:05:36,570
Though I am surprised
to find you back at work

116
00:05:36,736 --> 00:05:40,195
and not tracking down who
really did kill your lady love.

117
00:05:40,740 --> 00:05:42,540
That's because you
don't see the full picture.

118
00:05:43,276 --> 00:05:45,108
The mayor has many enemies.

119
00:05:45,278 --> 00:05:47,890
These enemies understand that I
am a fundamental part of this operation.

120
00:05:47,914 --> 00:05:49,712
They weaken me, they weaken him.

121
00:05:49,883 --> 00:05:52,478
That was clearly the
intent of killing Isabella.

122
00:05:53,453 --> 00:05:56,787
Also, I have spies
all over the city.

123
00:05:56,957 --> 00:06:00,086
Soon enough, whoever killed
Isabella will reveal themselves,

124
00:06:00,260 --> 00:06:02,559
and I will strike.

125
00:06:04,097 --> 00:06:05,725
Poor blind baby.

126
00:06:06,967 --> 00:06:10,995
It's always hardest to see
what's right under our noses.

127
00:06:13,006 --> 00:06:14,474
(COUGHS) Penguin!

128
00:06:19,646 --> 00:06:21,080
Did you just
fake-cough "Penguin"?

129
00:06:22,482 --> 00:06:23,482
(CHUCKLING)

130
00:06:23,783 --> 00:06:27,550
Needless to say, that is
absurd on a number of levels.

131
00:06:27,954 --> 00:06:29,388
Really?

132
00:06:29,556 --> 00:06:32,720
All a crime requires is
means, motive, and opportunity.

133
00:06:32,893 --> 00:06:36,955
And your beaky little buddy certainly
has the means and opportunity.

134
00:06:37,130 --> 00:06:38,655
But no motive.

135
00:06:38,832 --> 00:06:41,893
Oh, I would say he had
the oldest motive in the book.

136
00:06:43,069 --> 00:06:47,029
Rich men want it, wise men
know it, the poor all need it.

137
00:06:47,207 --> 00:06:49,802
Love. What does
that have to do...

138
00:06:53,914 --> 00:06:56,543
And the penny drops.

139
00:07:02,555 --> 00:07:04,615
You are suggesting

140
00:07:05,692 --> 00:07:09,720
that Oswald is in love with me.

141
00:07:11,298 --> 00:07:12,732
That is ridiculous.

142
00:07:12,899 --> 00:07:15,259
I know. I mean, personally,
I find you a bit of a cold fish.

143
00:07:15,402 --> 00:07:20,340
But Ozzie saw you being taken
away from him by that bookish vixen.

144
00:07:20,840 --> 00:07:21,864
<i>And...</i>

145
00:07:22,609 --> 00:07:24,510
(IMITATES ENGINE RUNNING)

146
00:07:25,879 --> 00:07:28,075
Oh, no!

147
00:07:30,250 --> 00:07:31,250
Hmm.

148
00:07:32,452 --> 00:07:33,681
No.

149
00:07:33,853 --> 00:07:37,187
In fact, I'm beginning to wonder
what your motive is in all this.

150
00:07:37,724 --> 00:07:39,750
That's for later.

151
00:07:40,393 --> 00:07:44,990
Right now, I just
wanna see justice

152
00:07:45,165 --> 00:07:48,260
for that poor sweet girl.

153
00:07:48,435 --> 00:07:52,736
Ms. Kean, I need you
to understand two things.

154
00:07:53,773 --> 00:07:57,175
One, Oswald did
not kill Isabella.

155
00:07:57,344 --> 00:08:00,610
And two, he is
not in love with me.

156
00:08:05,218 --> 00:08:06,516
Are you so certain?

157
00:08:07,721 --> 00:08:10,088
Don't you owe it
to her to find out?

158
00:08:12,258 --> 00:08:13,726
Let me know how it goes.

159
00:08:17,964 --> 00:08:20,695
The Court of Owls maintains a
number of buildings in Gotham.

160
00:08:20,867 --> 00:08:23,996
This one is rarely occupied.
But always well-guarded.

161
00:08:24,170 --> 00:08:26,969
<i>And there are two alarms.
The first covers points of entry.</i>

162
00:08:27,140 --> 00:08:29,234
Last week, we managed to
disarm one of the windows.

163
00:08:29,409 --> 00:08:32,868
Once inside, the front door can be
opened using a code that we possess.

164
00:08:33,279 --> 00:08:37,307
The second alarm is in the
basement, in the room with the safe.

165
00:08:37,484 --> 00:08:39,783
<i>The floor is fitted
with infrared sensors.</i>

166
00:08:39,953 --> 00:08:41,421
You must cross it on a rope.

167
00:08:43,123 --> 00:08:44,614
I have trained for this.

168
00:08:44,791 --> 00:08:47,431
You will give me the key you
found, and I will retrieve the object.

169
00:08:47,694 --> 00:08:49,959
But you still don't know
what the object is, right?

170
00:08:50,130 --> 00:08:53,294
Only that the Court
protects it. Fears it.

171
00:08:53,466 --> 00:08:56,561
And that with Talon
hunting us, we have no time.

172
00:09:02,342 --> 00:09:05,039
Right, so let's go
through this again.

173
00:09:05,211 --> 00:09:06,235
What'd you decide?

174
00:09:06,846 --> 00:09:10,339
We're gonna break in today.
We can't wait any longer.

175
00:09:12,552 --> 00:09:14,521
- You okay?
- Fine.

176
00:09:15,255 --> 00:09:16,348
Just hungry.

177
00:09:20,827 --> 00:09:21,827
JIM: <i>GCPD.</i>

178
00:09:23,763 --> 00:09:25,857
A guy named Ryan
Pfeffer work here?

179
00:09:26,166 --> 00:09:30,695
Uh, yeah. He's sub-level
3. What, he in trouble?

180
00:09:30,870 --> 00:09:33,362
He was killed last night. I
need to talk to his colleagues.

181
00:09:33,540 --> 00:09:35,340
You guys keep track of
when keycards are used?

182
00:09:35,508 --> 00:09:36,508
Uh, yeah.

183
00:09:36,676 --> 00:09:38,144
All right.

184
00:09:38,311 --> 00:09:39,802
If anybody uses his, call me.

185
00:09:39,979 --> 00:09:42,744
Sure, but his was
used 20 minutes ago.

186
00:09:44,284 --> 00:09:45,377
He hasn't logged out.

187
00:09:45,552 --> 00:09:47,180
Call the police. Now.

188
00:10:01,901 --> 00:10:03,836
(GRUNTING)

189
00:10:11,411 --> 00:10:13,004
(ALARM BLARING)

190
00:10:16,950 --> 00:10:17,950
Jim, Jim.

191
00:10:18,118 --> 00:10:22,852
You're ahead of schedule. Our
paths weren't meant to cross just yet.

192
00:10:27,694 --> 00:10:29,094
But I'm not gonna kill you yet.

193
00:10:29,696 --> 00:10:32,063
I do that, you
become the martyr.

194
00:10:32,232 --> 00:10:34,599
And she'll carry you
in her heart forever.

195
00:10:34,767 --> 00:10:36,827
<i>No. Before I kill you,</i>

196
00:10:37,504 --> 00:10:39,632
she has to hate you.

197
00:10:40,306 --> 00:10:41,306
And she will.

198
00:10:45,745 --> 00:10:47,270
Come find me, Jim.

199
00:10:53,620 --> 00:10:56,681
So you didn't get a look at the
guy. And he's not on the cameras.

200
00:10:56,856 --> 00:10:58,400
We might get something
off the prints, but...

201
00:10:58,424 --> 00:11:01,360
Doubtful, if he was smart enough
to avoid the cameras. I'm good.

202
00:11:01,528 --> 00:11:04,589
He seems to have been interested in
the research into Alice Tetch's blood.

203
00:11:04,764 --> 00:11:07,256
Pfeffer's office was ransacked
and their files were missing.

204
00:11:07,433 --> 00:11:11,063
So someone else is infected
with the virus? That's just great.

205
00:11:11,237 --> 00:11:13,449
It isn't you, is it? Because that
sure would make things easy.

206
00:11:13,473 --> 00:11:16,409
No. It's not me. What's
that on your hand?

207
00:11:17,544 --> 00:11:19,445
"Arkham." I didn't write it.

208
00:11:19,612 --> 00:11:20,944
<i>Okay, let's all just calm down.</i>

209
00:11:21,114 --> 00:11:23,310
So the virus-infected
killer wrote on your hand.

210
00:11:23,783 --> 00:11:25,445
He wants you to go to Arkham.

211
00:11:25,618 --> 00:11:26,711
Barnes is in Arkham.

212
00:11:27,086 --> 00:11:29,521
No. It's not about Barnes.

213
00:11:30,590 --> 00:11:32,923
- Jim, you okay?
- Yeah, I'm fine.

214
00:11:34,460 --> 00:11:35,985
(DOOR ALARM BUZZES)

215
00:11:40,934 --> 00:11:43,096
- Hello, Jervis.
- James.

216
00:11:43,836 --> 00:11:45,634
What an unexpected pleasure.

217
00:11:48,441 --> 00:11:51,104
Someone else is infected
with your sister's blood.

218
00:11:51,277 --> 00:11:52,277
You don't say!

219
00:11:52,445 --> 00:11:57,110
And I've been thinking, it's possible
she infected them accidentally.

220
00:11:57,884 --> 00:12:00,854
Yes, possible, possible.

221
00:12:01,020 --> 00:12:03,251
But your reaction
tells me you knew.

222
00:12:03,423 --> 00:12:07,451
So, you infected them after
you stole your sister's blood.

223
00:12:08,261 --> 00:12:11,925
But you stayed quiet, waiting
for them to show symptoms.

224
00:12:12,098 --> 00:12:15,626
Well, that would be darn
sneaky of me, wouldn't it?

225
00:12:16,302 --> 00:12:18,237
I need the name.

226
00:12:18,538 --> 00:12:21,406
(CHUCKLING) You need the name.

227
00:12:22,542 --> 00:12:25,171
So, I've been quiet
about it all this time,

228
00:12:25,345 --> 00:12:27,644
and now I'm going to help you,

229
00:12:27,814 --> 00:12:29,783
because we're such good friends?

230
00:12:29,949 --> 00:12:32,384
Because I can make your
life here very uncomfortable.

231
00:12:32,552 --> 00:12:35,021
More uncomfortable than
having Captain Barnes next door

232
00:12:35,188 --> 00:12:37,885
screaming, "Guilty!"
all hours of the night?

233
00:12:38,057 --> 00:12:39,320
Give me the name!

234
00:12:39,559 --> 00:12:44,998
(CHUCKLING) Oh, James, I would love
to see what Alice's virus would do to you.

235
00:12:45,164 --> 00:12:50,762
The beast in you is right
there, so desperate to get out.

236
00:12:53,740 --> 00:12:57,507
And I know of whom you
speak, oh, yes, indeed.

237
00:12:57,677 --> 00:13:00,340
I stabbed him and pricked
him and caused him to bleed.

238
00:13:00,513 --> 00:13:01,776
<i>But nothing you can say,</i>

239
00:13:01,948 --> 00:13:05,248
<i>no words you might possess can
pry from me the smallest guess.</i>

240
00:13:05,418 --> 00:13:08,081
For this game is my game.

241
00:13:08,254 --> 00:13:10,018
I say when it's done.

242
00:13:10,823 --> 00:13:13,418
And right now I'm
having too much fun.

243
00:13:15,762 --> 00:13:17,253
You wanna play a game, Jervis?

244
00:13:18,097 --> 00:13:19,793
Fine. Let's play a game.

245
00:13:21,534 --> 00:13:25,904
Whoever you infected
has some sort of plan.

246
00:13:27,307 --> 00:13:29,435
I want you to tell me
the name of this man.

247
00:13:31,277 --> 00:13:36,272
Well, James, I have
to give that effort an F.

248
00:13:37,250 --> 00:13:38,718
And can you really
imagine that...

249
00:13:38,885 --> 00:13:42,049
Two are dead. More may die soon.

250
00:13:42,221 --> 00:13:44,554
This isn't a game,
give me his name.

251
00:13:44,724 --> 00:13:46,484
You'll only know his
name when it's too late,

252
00:13:46,592 --> 00:13:48,493
when the one you love
has been murdered by hate.

253
00:13:50,063 --> 00:13:51,588
Guard! Take me to my cell!

254
00:13:51,764 --> 00:13:53,733
- What do you mean "the one that I love"?
- Guard!

255
00:13:53,900 --> 00:13:56,768
Give me his name, Tetch. Give me
his name! Or you share the blame!

256
00:13:56,936 --> 00:13:58,247
Nothing! Nothing!
I'll tell you naught!

257
00:13:58,271 --> 00:13:59,748
His name shall be
neither spoken nor taught.

258
00:13:59,772 --> 00:14:02,012
He'll cut, and he'll crush,
and the blood will run thick!

259
00:14:02,075 --> 00:14:05,375
Though from healer to killer
is no easy trick! (GROANS)

260
00:14:05,812 --> 00:14:07,781
"Healer to killer."

261
00:14:08,681 --> 00:14:10,172
He's a doctor.

262
00:14:11,351 --> 00:14:12,478
Oh, my God.

263
00:14:12,652 --> 00:14:14,280
You'll never stop him, James!

264
00:14:14,454 --> 00:14:16,685
He'll kill, and he'll
kill, and he'll kill!

265
00:14:16,856 --> 00:14:19,016
This is Jim Gordon. Get me
Dr. Mario Calvi immediately.

266
00:14:19,525 --> 00:14:22,689
On my damn
authority! Just do it!

267
00:14:34,607 --> 00:14:36,667
ALFRED: I take it you're off.

268
00:14:36,909 --> 00:14:37,909
(SIGHS)

269
00:14:39,078 --> 00:14:43,072
When we were casing that place, I
got a feeling we were being watched.

270
00:14:44,384 --> 00:14:46,478
And if this Court of
Owls is all you say,

271
00:14:46,652 --> 00:14:49,315
they're not gonna be too cool
with Bruce breaking their deal.

272
00:14:49,489 --> 00:14:51,355
That's very true.

273
00:14:52,225 --> 00:14:56,993
But Master Bruce knows the Court
will catch up with him sooner or later.

274
00:14:57,163 --> 00:14:59,908
<i>And if he has the opportunity to take
them out, then he will take them out.</i>

275
00:14:59,932 --> 00:15:01,161
That's a big "if."

276
00:15:01,334 --> 00:15:04,133
Especially when your stupid job
is supposed to be protecting him.

277
00:15:04,303 --> 00:15:05,601
My stupid job, miss,

278
00:15:05,772 --> 00:15:09,641
is to make sure that he grows
up to be the man he's meant to be.

279
00:15:10,810 --> 00:15:12,005
Still.

280
00:15:12,712 --> 00:15:16,479
Kind of a punk move for him to make a deal
with the people who killed his parents.

281
00:15:16,649 --> 00:15:18,129
Yeah, well, you
understand this then.

282
00:15:20,086 --> 00:15:23,181
He only did what he did to
protect the people he cares about.

283
00:15:24,624 --> 00:15:26,183
<i>For you.</i>

284
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:29,095
And it cost him dearly.

285
00:15:36,202 --> 00:15:39,263
Are you serious? Arresting Don
Falcone's son on his wedding day?

286
00:15:39,439 --> 00:15:41,032
I had no choice.
He's got the virus.

287
00:15:41,207 --> 00:15:43,870
Do you really think Lee
Thompkins, <i>Dr.</i> Lee Thompkins,

288
00:15:44,043 --> 00:15:45,978
wouldn't know if her
own fiancé had the virus?

289
00:15:46,145 --> 00:15:48,239
How long did Barnes
have it and hide it?

290
00:15:48,414 --> 00:15:51,441
Tetch must have infected him that
night in the hospital when he dosed me.

291
00:15:51,617 --> 00:15:53,210
- It would explain things.
- Like what?

292
00:15:53,586 --> 00:15:55,226
Mario hitting me at
the engagement party.

293
00:15:55,254 --> 00:15:57,018
You know what also
would explain that?

294
00:15:57,190 --> 00:15:59,591
You telling Tetch
to shoot his fiancée.

295
00:15:59,759 --> 00:16:02,438
You should've seen his face when
those assassins attacked us, his rage.

296
00:16:02,462 --> 00:16:04,055
He was being
attacked by assassins!

297
00:16:04,230 --> 00:16:06,575
What was I supposed to do,
Harvey? Wait until he kills again?

298
00:16:06,599 --> 00:16:07,623
Till he hurts Lee?

299
00:16:07,800 --> 00:16:09,845
You were supposed to wait
until you had enough proof.

300
00:16:09,869 --> 00:16:13,101
And why would Tetch
infect Mario in the first place?

301
00:16:13,272 --> 00:16:14,331
To hurt me.

302
00:16:14,507 --> 00:16:16,987
Okay, let's say you're right.
Let's say that Mario is infected.

303
00:16:17,076 --> 00:16:19,978
<i>So he crushes some guy's
skull. He breaks into the lab.</i>

304
00:16:20,146 --> 00:16:23,583
He attacks you and then he
writes "Arkham" on your hand?

305
00:16:23,749 --> 00:16:26,344
Why would he
want you to find him?

306
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:28,720
I don't know.

307
00:16:30,490 --> 00:16:31,685
He doesn't have the virus.

308
00:16:31,858 --> 00:16:33,554
What? No, no, no. Run it again.

309
00:16:33,726 --> 00:16:35,820
I ran it three
times. He's clean.

310
00:16:36,496 --> 00:16:39,056
I could've told you that.
But, hey, I'm glad it's official.

311
00:16:39,732 --> 00:16:42,395
Dr. Calvi, on
behalf of the GCPD,

312
00:16:42,568 --> 00:16:43,900
I just want to apologize for any

313
00:16:44,604 --> 00:16:46,971
inconvenience or embarrassment
this may have caused you.

314
00:16:47,139 --> 00:16:50,803
No need. Living with Lee, I understand
the pressures you're all under.

315
00:16:50,977 --> 00:16:53,446
But if you'll excuse me, I
have a wedding to attend.

316
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:55,173
<i>Jim.</i>

317
00:16:55,348 --> 00:16:57,715
I understand this is
a tough day for you.

318
00:16:57,884 --> 00:16:59,512
But no hard feelings.

319
00:16:59,685 --> 00:17:02,450
The test. That's why
you broke into the lab.

320
00:17:02,622 --> 00:17:03,817
To find out how to beat it.

321
00:17:03,990 --> 00:17:05,049
- But why?
- Jim...

322
00:17:05,224 --> 00:17:07,216
I know you have the
virus. I'm gonna prove it.

323
00:17:07,393 --> 00:17:09,362
And I promise you
will never marry Lee.

324
00:17:15,434 --> 00:17:16,554
But she didn't say anything?

325
00:17:16,702 --> 00:17:19,035
She said she thought
we were being watched.

326
00:17:20,206 --> 00:17:23,233
Personally I think
she's just got the jitters.

327
00:17:23,976 --> 00:17:25,069
She can't still be mad

328
00:17:25,278 --> 00:17:27,406
- I told Ivy she was my girlfriend.
- (GROANS) Oh.

329
00:17:28,080 --> 00:17:30,743
It just slipped out. She can
call herself whatever she wants.

330
00:17:30,917 --> 00:17:33,837
Fascinating as I find this tale of
young unrequited love is, Master Bruce,

331
00:17:33,986 --> 00:17:36,979
please can we just
concentrate on the task at hand?

332
00:17:37,156 --> 00:17:38,385
Do you have the key?

333
00:17:39,492 --> 00:17:41,085
Excellent.

334
00:17:41,260 --> 00:17:44,230
Alfred, you know when we
get this thing, whatever it is,

335
00:17:44,897 --> 00:17:46,697
the Whispers are gonna
try to take it from us.

336
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:48,732
Well, to be honest,
Master Bruce,

337
00:17:49,702 --> 00:17:51,398
it's not the Whispers
I'm worried about.

338
00:18:04,951 --> 00:18:06,783
(GASPING AND CHOKING)

339
00:18:09,155 --> 00:18:12,922
And have we made any headway
on the waterfront negotiations?

340
00:18:13,092 --> 00:18:14,403
ED: I've spoken
with the union leader.

341
00:18:14,427 --> 00:18:15,759
He agreed to our offer.

342
00:18:15,928 --> 00:18:18,227
So those photos can
go back in the vault.

343
00:18:19,498 --> 00:18:21,109
- They were quite saucy, weren't they?
- (BOTH CHUCKLE)

344
00:18:21,133 --> 00:18:22,133
And how about the...

345
00:18:22,301 --> 00:18:24,861
Your approval for the new casino
should come through tomorrow.

346
00:18:25,237 --> 00:18:27,536
Demolition can begin right away.

347
00:18:27,707 --> 00:18:30,939
Ed, I cannot tell you how good it
is to see you back to your old self.

348
00:18:32,478 --> 00:18:34,071
Just one last signature.

349
00:18:39,185 --> 00:18:40,551
This is your resignation.

350
00:18:41,921 --> 00:18:44,288
Isabella's death has altered
things and I can't continue...

351
00:18:44,457 --> 00:18:47,916
No! Ed, I will
not let you leave!

352
00:18:49,996 --> 00:18:51,897
It is not in your best interest.

353
00:18:53,165 --> 00:18:54,656
You have to stay busy.

354
00:18:58,938 --> 00:19:00,338
How can I say this?

355
00:19:02,508 --> 00:19:03,999
We're friends.

356
00:19:06,245 --> 00:19:08,009
- Aren't we, Oswald?
- Huh?

357
00:19:08,681 --> 00:19:09,808
Of course!

358
00:19:11,117 --> 00:19:12,585
Since the accident...

359
00:19:13,319 --> 00:19:16,221
And I never thought
that this could happen.

360
00:19:18,457 --> 00:19:23,088
I've had the desire to become
more than employer-employee.

361
00:19:25,431 --> 00:19:26,865
More than friends.

362
00:19:31,270 --> 00:19:33,034
I have been feeling the same.

363
00:19:34,440 --> 00:19:35,533
I didn't wanna mention it

364
00:19:35,708 --> 00:19:37,768
because of all the
awfulness about Isabelle.

365
00:19:37,943 --> 00:19:39,206
- Isabella.
- (GULPS)

366
00:19:40,346 --> 00:19:41,346
But...

367
00:19:44,283 --> 00:19:46,081
One cannot deny love.

368
00:19:46,318 --> 00:19:47,616
(GASPS)

369
00:19:49,889 --> 00:19:52,358
What is it? What's wrong?

370
00:19:53,225 --> 00:19:54,420
There...

371
00:19:55,795 --> 00:19:57,093
There's been a misunderstanding.

372
00:19:58,531 --> 00:20:02,229
I was going to propose
that we become partners.

373
00:20:03,836 --> 00:20:05,464
Business partners.

374
00:20:06,739 --> 00:20:08,002
Partners.

375
00:20:09,675 --> 00:20:11,405
- Then...
- Excuse me.

376
00:20:14,213 --> 00:20:15,374
(DOOR OPENS)

377
00:20:19,885 --> 00:20:21,376
Lee? You here? It's Jim!

378
00:20:21,554 --> 00:20:22,554
MARIO: <i>Hello, Jim.</i>

379
00:20:23,055 --> 00:20:24,785
I saw you left Lee a message.

380
00:20:24,957 --> 00:20:27,654
I, uh, accidentally took
her phone this morning.

381
00:20:28,160 --> 00:20:30,095
<i>She's not here, by the way.</i>

382
00:20:30,262 --> 00:20:31,992
- Drink?
- No, thanks.

383
00:20:32,164 --> 00:20:33,689
How'd you pass the test?

384
00:20:36,435 --> 00:20:38,563
Because I don't have the virus.

385
00:20:39,505 --> 00:20:40,505
Or do I?

386
00:20:44,176 --> 00:20:46,077
You're gonna arrest me, Jim?

387
00:20:46,245 --> 00:20:49,044
You wanna look even more
like the paranoid ex-lover?

388
00:20:49,215 --> 00:20:50,683
I'll only pass the test again.

389
00:20:50,850 --> 00:20:54,446
We'll find out how you
beat it. Only a matter of time.

390
00:20:55,187 --> 00:20:58,316
Let's say I do have the virus.
How would I have gotten it?

391
00:20:58,491 --> 00:21:01,791
From Tetch. When he
dosed me with hallucinogen.

392
00:21:02,628 --> 00:21:06,998
JERVIS: <i>Dr. Calvi, I'd like
you to meet my sister, Alice.</i>

393
00:21:07,900 --> 00:21:11,803
With Barnes, the virus
stoked his anger at the guilty.

394
00:21:12,838 --> 00:21:14,966
What dark part of me
has it brought to life?

395
00:21:15,141 --> 00:21:16,575
Jealousy.

396
00:21:17,877 --> 00:21:19,573
You're afraid of losing Lee.

397
00:21:20,146 --> 00:21:21,910
If that's true,

398
00:21:22,081 --> 00:21:25,540
that means the woman
we both know you still love

399
00:21:25,718 --> 00:21:29,883
is gonna marry a lunatic
who'll do anything to keep her.

400
00:21:31,290 --> 00:21:32,986
Are you sure you
don't want that drink?

401
00:21:33,159 --> 00:21:35,993
What I wanna know is
why you put me on your trail.

402
00:21:36,162 --> 00:21:37,289
What are you after?

403
00:21:37,863 --> 00:21:38,956
Let me give you a hint.

404
00:21:40,032 --> 00:21:44,436
You see, what keeps me up at night
is not the thought that you love her.

405
00:21:45,538 --> 00:21:49,441
It's the thought that a
part of her still loves you.

406
00:21:50,976 --> 00:21:53,639
Well, in that
case, let's find her.

407
00:21:53,813 --> 00:21:56,146
Let her decide if
she's gonna marry you.

408
00:21:58,050 --> 00:22:00,281
Yeah, I don't think so.

409
00:22:04,023 --> 00:22:06,993
The virus made you strong,
not bulletproof. Let's go.

410
00:22:07,159 --> 00:22:08,991
You know what, Jim,
with all this virus talk,

411
00:22:09,161 --> 00:22:10,595
<i>you keep forgetting one thing.</i>

412
00:22:11,130 --> 00:22:13,565
I'm still Carmine Falcone's son.

413
00:22:15,668 --> 00:22:16,966
You know Victor.

414
00:22:17,203 --> 00:22:18,203
(GRUNTS)

415
00:22:19,371 --> 00:22:20,703
Hi-ho.

416
00:22:27,446 --> 00:22:29,438
JIM: <i>Victor, were
you listening to him?</i>

417
00:22:29,615 --> 00:22:31,208
He has the same
virus as Barnes had!

418
00:22:31,917 --> 00:22:34,944
What's that? Oh,
no. I wasn't listening.

419
00:22:35,120 --> 00:22:36,748
- You have to let me go.
- Uh-huh?

420
00:22:38,190 --> 00:22:39,750
- Does Falcone know you're here?
- Wait.

421
00:22:40,492 --> 00:22:42,017
Wait.

422
00:22:45,431 --> 00:22:46,956
You're free to go, Jim.

423
00:22:48,634 --> 00:22:49,634
(BULLET CLATTERS)

424
00:22:49,835 --> 00:22:50,859
I'll keep this.

425
00:22:52,671 --> 00:22:53,671
I don't understand.

426
00:22:53,839 --> 00:22:55,079
I was only supposed to keep you

427
00:22:55,107 --> 00:22:57,770
until the big hand was on
nine and the little hand...

428
00:22:57,943 --> 00:22:59,377
My mag. Now.

429
00:22:59,545 --> 00:23:00,706
Sorry, Jim.

430
00:23:00,880 --> 00:23:02,781
But hey, give the
bride a kiss for me.

431
00:23:03,482 --> 00:23:04,482
(GRUNTS)

432
00:23:05,351 --> 00:23:06,580
I asked.

433
00:23:11,690 --> 00:23:15,149
And it is with great pleasure
that I present this award

434
00:23:15,327 --> 00:23:18,161
to Mr. Kyle Davis for
his magnificent book,

435
00:23:19,298 --> 00:23:21,995
<i>Gotham's Sewers:
an Oral History.</i>

436
00:23:22,601 --> 00:23:24,661
Looks just fascinating.

437
00:23:24,904 --> 00:23:26,065
(CHEERS AND APPLAUSE)

438
00:23:26,305 --> 00:23:27,603
Thank you.

439
00:23:28,173 --> 00:23:30,233
<i>Oh, you're too kind. I love...</i>

440
00:23:30,509 --> 00:23:31,772
- (GRUNTS)
- (SCREAMS)

441
00:23:32,211 --> 00:23:33,406
(ALL CLAMORING)

442
00:23:34,380 --> 00:23:36,474
(APPLAUSE CONTINUES)

443
00:23:42,621 --> 00:23:43,987
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

444
00:23:45,658 --> 00:23:46,751
Ed.

445
00:23:48,527 --> 00:23:50,496
I was worried when you ran off.

446
00:23:50,663 --> 00:23:52,825
That I might have upset you.

447
00:23:54,967 --> 00:23:57,129
Can't we just pretend
that nothing happened?

448
00:23:57,303 --> 00:23:59,829
Just go back to the
way things were?

449
00:24:04,443 --> 00:24:07,072
You are the best
friend I've ever had.

450
00:24:08,614 --> 00:24:10,515
I don't wanna lose you.

451
00:24:10,950 --> 00:24:12,145
(BREATHING RAGGEDLY)

452
00:24:12,418 --> 00:24:13,613
<i>Please.</i>

453
00:24:17,056 --> 00:24:18,786
You're my best
friend as well, Oswald.

454
00:24:21,760 --> 00:24:23,251
Remember that.

455
00:24:41,413 --> 00:24:42,881
Jim, what are you doing here?

456
00:24:43,048 --> 00:24:44,880
Are you okay?

457
00:24:45,050 --> 00:24:46,279
Where's Mario?

458
00:24:46,452 --> 00:24:48,717
He's out at the church.
We're about to get married!

459
00:24:50,422 --> 00:24:51,515
You can't marry him.

460
00:24:51,690 --> 00:24:53,124
Oh, my God.

461
00:24:54,126 --> 00:24:56,322
- Just give us a minute.
- Yeah.

462
00:24:56,528 --> 00:24:57,587
(DOOR OPENS)

463
00:25:06,305 --> 00:25:08,740
Listen to me. And I know
how this is gonna sound.

464
00:25:08,907 --> 00:25:11,376
You think that he
has Alice Tetch's virus.

465
00:25:12,244 --> 00:25:13,644
- He told you.
- Yes.

466
00:25:13,812 --> 00:25:17,579
And he told me that you had him
arrested today. On our wedding day.

467
00:25:17,750 --> 00:25:20,379
And you had Lucius give him the
test three times. And he passed.

468
00:25:20,886 --> 00:25:23,856
- What's wrong with you?
- He cheated the test, Lee.

469
00:25:24,023 --> 00:25:25,286
I don't know how. But he did.

470
00:25:25,457 --> 00:25:27,551
Tetch infected him
that night in the hospital.

471
00:25:27,726 --> 00:25:29,086
You went to see
Tetch, didn't you?

472
00:25:29,495 --> 00:25:30,495
Yes.

473
00:25:30,662 --> 00:25:33,655
Jim, don't you see? Tetch is
planting ideas in your head.

474
00:25:33,832 --> 00:25:34,891
- No.
- Don't you remember?

475
00:25:35,067 --> 00:25:37,332
- He's done this before.
- No. This isn't like that.

476
00:25:37,770 --> 00:25:38,999
Okay, what is more likely?

477
00:25:39,171 --> 00:25:41,606
That Tetch is planting ideas
in your head to screw with you,

478
00:25:41,774 --> 00:25:43,538
or that Mario has Alice's virus?

479
00:25:43,709 --> 00:25:45,701
Lee, you cannot marry him!

480
00:25:47,012 --> 00:25:50,505
Mario said that you would
never let us be happy.

481
00:25:50,682 --> 00:25:52,947
I thought he was
overreacting. But he's right.

482
00:25:53,118 --> 00:25:56,816
Tetch or not, you are obsessed.

483
00:25:57,489 --> 00:25:58,718
Let it go!

484
00:26:01,160 --> 00:26:02,321
This is what he wanted.

485
00:26:02,494 --> 00:26:03,860
What are you talking about?

486
00:26:04,029 --> 00:26:05,827
This. Me coming here.

487
00:26:06,899 --> 00:26:09,835
That's why he
put me on his trail.

488
00:26:10,002 --> 00:26:12,801
He got the test so he
could find out how to beat it,

489
00:26:13,605 --> 00:26:16,905
he had me arrest him so
I'd look like a jealous ex.

490
00:26:17,509 --> 00:26:20,172
That's why Zsasz let
me go, so I'd race here.

491
00:26:22,081 --> 00:26:23,640
And finally push you away.

492
00:26:24,016 --> 00:26:25,382
Oh, Jim.

493
00:26:26,118 --> 00:26:29,088
I say this as someone
who cares about you.

494
00:26:30,022 --> 00:26:32,082
Get help.

495
00:26:37,963 --> 00:26:39,329
I love you.

496
00:26:45,037 --> 00:26:46,096
I love you.

497
00:26:47,072 --> 00:26:48,301
I've never stopped.

498
00:26:50,209 --> 00:26:52,529
I should've come to see you
as soon as I got out of prison,

499
00:26:52,578 --> 00:26:54,103
but I couldn't.

500
00:26:54,847 --> 00:26:55,974
I was ashamed.

501
00:26:57,549 --> 00:26:59,780
I felt I had to
set things right.

502
00:26:59,952 --> 00:27:02,683
But I did finally come, Lee.

503
00:27:05,791 --> 00:27:09,956
I saw you through
the window with him.

504
00:27:10,863 --> 00:27:12,263
You were smiling.

505
00:27:12,431 --> 00:27:14,059
You looked happy.

506
00:27:17,236 --> 00:27:18,829
I couldn't bring
myself to go in.

507
00:27:20,038 --> 00:27:22,269
I've regretted it
every day since.

508
00:27:23,542 --> 00:27:24,737
Please.

509
00:27:28,080 --> 00:27:29,241
Don't marry him.

510
00:27:37,856 --> 00:27:39,688
After the wedding,

511
00:27:41,293 --> 00:27:43,387
Mario and I are leaving Gotham.

512
00:27:44,696 --> 00:27:46,927
I'll never see you again.

513
00:27:47,099 --> 00:27:48,624
- Lee...
- Damn you.

514
00:27:49,234 --> 00:27:52,033
For telling me this now!

515
00:27:52,938 --> 00:27:55,138
(SOBBING) You come in here
with these crazy accusations,

516
00:27:55,274 --> 00:27:58,176
and when I don't
believe you, you pull this?

517
00:27:58,343 --> 00:27:59,811
How dare you? (GRUNTS)

518
00:28:04,816 --> 00:28:06,307
Don't you see?

519
00:28:07,553 --> 00:28:10,284
- He wants you to hate me.
- Well, he succeeded.

520
00:28:10,455 --> 00:28:12,583
- Get the hell out of here!
- No!

521
00:28:12,791 --> 00:28:14,384
(SIGHS) Fine.

522
00:28:14,560 --> 00:28:15,960
Carmine.

523
00:28:17,162 --> 00:28:19,563
Can you please help
Detective Gordon find the exit?

524
00:28:19,731 --> 00:28:21,063
Certainly.

525
00:28:23,869 --> 00:28:25,667
And if you're ready, my dear...

526
00:28:28,240 --> 00:28:29,503
I am.

527
00:29:19,925 --> 00:29:22,121
PRIEST: <i>Do you, Leslie,
take Mario to be your husband?</i>

528
00:29:23,228 --> 00:29:24,491
I do.

529
00:29:27,499 --> 00:29:28,660
(GRUNTING)

530
00:29:29,401 --> 00:29:31,632
And do you, Mario, take
Leslie to be your wife?

531
00:29:32,471 --> 00:29:33,564
I do.

532
00:29:37,609 --> 00:29:39,976
PRIEST: <i>I now pronounce
you husband and wife.</i>

533
00:29:40,445 --> 00:29:41,708
You may kiss the bride.

534
00:30:04,803 --> 00:30:07,864
Ladies and gentlemen,
Mr. and Mrs. Calvi.

535
00:30:08,073 --> 00:30:10,338
(CHEERS AND APPLAUSE)

536
00:30:33,465 --> 00:30:35,297
Well, I think it's
safe to admit that

537
00:30:35,467 --> 00:30:37,561
our foreign friends are a
no-show, Master Bruce.

538
00:30:37,736 --> 00:30:39,466
It was a right
dodgy plan, anyway.

539
00:30:39,638 --> 00:30:42,164
- Where are you going?
- That would be home.

540
00:30:42,574 --> 00:30:44,770
Alfred, this is our only
shot to take down the Court.

541
00:30:44,943 --> 00:30:47,663
Yeah, well, you don't know that,
do you? I mean, it was a moot point.

542
00:30:47,813 --> 00:30:50,858
Anyway. I mean, walking across the entire
length of a room on a bloody tightrope?

543
00:30:50,882 --> 00:30:52,111
I can do it. I did it.

544
00:30:52,284 --> 00:30:55,448
Yeah. Three times out of 20. I
counted. No, thank you very much.

545
00:30:55,620 --> 00:30:57,020
I can do it.

546
00:30:58,457 --> 00:31:00,858
Oh, that's bloody
marvelous, isn't it?

547
00:31:01,026 --> 00:31:02,050
Hey?

548
00:31:05,097 --> 00:31:09,865
Right. The deal is this. You
stay on comms, at all times.

549
00:31:10,035 --> 00:31:13,096
If I order "abort," you
abort. Is that clear?

550
00:31:13,271 --> 00:31:16,605
- I need my head examined. I really do.
- (SELINA SCOFFS)

551
00:31:17,376 --> 00:31:18,537
(ZIPPING UP)

552
00:31:20,278 --> 00:31:21,278
What?

553
00:31:22,214 --> 00:31:23,739
Just wondering.

554
00:31:26,284 --> 00:31:28,344
Does this mean
you are my girlfriend?

555
00:31:28,520 --> 00:31:29,681
Shut up.

556
00:31:38,830 --> 00:31:41,197
So, I thought if I were Mario,
how would I beat the test?

557
00:31:41,366 --> 00:31:43,411
Well, the test looks for
this one marker in the blood.

558
00:31:43,435 --> 00:31:46,337
But that marker can be masked by
an abundance of certain other drugs.

559
00:31:46,505 --> 00:31:48,838
The two most easily
available, Cloracinamine and...

560
00:31:49,007 --> 00:31:50,839
Lucius, just get to the point.

561
00:31:51,009 --> 00:31:53,774
Mario's blood came back off
the charts for Cloracinamine.

562
00:31:55,113 --> 00:31:58,880
Alvarez, get a unit on Lee
Thompkins and Dr. Mario Calvi!

563
00:31:59,050 --> 00:32:00,328
And don't let 'em
out of your sight!

564
00:32:00,352 --> 00:32:02,287
This isn't proof that
Mario killed those men.

565
00:32:02,454 --> 00:32:04,855
No, but it's enough
for a search warrant.

566
00:32:05,023 --> 00:32:06,719
Now I gotta go find Jim Gordon.

567
00:32:07,692 --> 00:32:09,957
GOON: Don't mess with Falcone!

568
00:32:10,262 --> 00:32:11,855
(TIRES SCREECHING)

569
00:32:15,634 --> 00:32:17,660
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

570
00:32:22,307 --> 00:32:23,536
(CAR ENGINE REVVING)

571
00:32:23,809 --> 00:32:25,038
(TIRES SCREECHING)

572
00:32:25,477 --> 00:32:26,638
(HORN BLARING)

573
00:32:37,889 --> 00:32:39,016
Hey.

574
00:32:40,492 --> 00:32:41,687
(GRUNTS)

575
00:33:03,615 --> 00:33:04,776
(BEEPING)

576
00:33:09,221 --> 00:33:12,282
All right. Straight to the safe room.
I'm gonna check the rest of the house.

577
00:33:12,457 --> 00:33:14,119
- Go on.
- This way.

578
00:33:23,468 --> 00:33:25,801
Not exactly hiding it.

579
00:33:26,671 --> 00:33:29,231
There's no point.
The floor is alarmed.

580
00:33:39,584 --> 00:33:40,813
(HEAVY BREATHING)

581
00:33:42,988 --> 00:33:45,981
Don't let go.

582
00:34:07,579 --> 00:34:08,579
- (GASPS)
- (GRUNTS)

583
00:34:23,695 --> 00:34:25,129
(STRAINING)

584
00:34:39,110 --> 00:34:40,110
(LOCK CLICKS)

585
00:35:07,439 --> 00:35:09,999
- (GRUNTS)
- (ALARM BLARING)

586
00:35:15,547 --> 00:35:16,674
(GRUNTS)

587
00:35:18,917 --> 00:35:21,045
- (GRUNTS)
- Come on!

588
00:35:25,056 --> 00:35:26,649
Out the way you came!

589
00:35:32,030 --> 00:35:33,030
- Let's go!
- No!

590
00:35:33,832 --> 00:35:35,460
(GRUNTING)

591
00:35:39,204 --> 00:35:40,365
No!

592
00:35:44,776 --> 00:35:45,776
Ah!

593
00:35:56,021 --> 00:35:57,284
(GRUNTING)

594
00:36:11,469 --> 00:36:12,596
(CHOKES)

595
00:36:14,139 --> 00:36:15,607
We have to leave.

596
00:36:15,774 --> 00:36:17,242
And who exactly are you?

597
00:36:17,842 --> 00:36:19,902
You're the one who's
been following us.

598
00:36:26,818 --> 00:36:28,116
Hey.

599
00:36:30,522 --> 00:36:32,184
You know her?

600
00:36:33,625 --> 00:36:34,625
That's my mom.

601
00:36:37,028 --> 00:36:38,189
Now can we get out of here?

602
00:36:38,363 --> 00:36:39,695
You're bloody right.

603
00:36:48,973 --> 00:36:52,307
- Found it! In his trash. Cloracinamine.
- (CAMERA SHUTTERS CLICKING)

604
00:36:52,777 --> 00:36:54,143
Oh, yes.

605
00:36:55,213 --> 00:36:56,875
We got him. Tell Alvarez.

606
00:36:57,048 --> 00:37:01,986
That was Alvarez. Lee and Mario
snuck out of the reception. He lost them.

607
00:37:04,756 --> 00:37:05,951
(TABITHA GRUNTING)

608
00:37:09,828 --> 00:37:12,992
I can't even hold a knife. I
swear, when I see Nygma...

609
00:37:13,164 --> 00:37:15,292
We'll kill him
together. Real slow.

610
00:37:15,467 --> 00:37:17,129
How sweet.

611
00:37:23,908 --> 00:37:25,433
You son of a bitch!

612
00:37:25,610 --> 00:37:28,478
Hear him out. Please.

613
00:37:40,825 --> 00:37:42,851
I don't want to kill him.

614
00:37:47,799 --> 00:37:50,064
I want to destroy him!

615
00:37:51,336 --> 00:37:54,135
I want to take away

616
00:37:55,373 --> 00:37:57,239
everything that he loves!

617
00:37:58,042 --> 00:38:00,170
I want to make him

618
00:38:01,646 --> 00:38:02,944
despised!

619
00:38:03,114 --> 00:38:04,309
What're you talking about?

620
00:38:04,482 --> 00:38:05,643
Penguin.

621
00:38:08,553 --> 00:38:10,852
- He killed the librarian.
- What?

622
00:38:12,223 --> 00:38:14,385
And you cut off my hand?

623
00:38:14,559 --> 00:38:16,323
I assume you want something.

624
00:38:17,061 --> 00:38:19,997
With Penguin gone, the
underworld will need a new leader.

625
00:38:21,800 --> 00:38:24,895
I think it's time Gotham
had a woman's touch.

626
00:38:25,069 --> 00:38:26,731
The crime families
will never follow you.

627
00:38:26,905 --> 00:38:30,501
Well, that's where you come in.
You know the families in and out.

628
00:38:30,675 --> 00:38:33,509
Not to mention you're
a whiz at strategy.

629
00:38:35,146 --> 00:38:36,910
Think about it, Ed.

630
00:38:37,782 --> 00:38:40,775
Your brains, their brawn,

631
00:38:41,753 --> 00:38:44,951
my... Me.

632
00:38:46,057 --> 00:38:47,582
We could make quite a team.

633
00:38:52,597 --> 00:38:54,327
We destroy Penguin first.

634
00:38:54,732 --> 00:38:56,098
'Course.

635
00:38:57,001 --> 00:38:59,630
But there is one
thing you need to do.

636
00:39:05,310 --> 00:39:06,437
Okay.

637
00:39:10,748 --> 00:39:11,841
(CLEARS THROAT)

638
00:39:14,052 --> 00:39:16,248
- I'm sorry about your hand.
- Apology not accepted.

639
00:39:16,421 --> 00:39:19,482
Well, we'll work
on that. Drinks!

640
00:39:23,628 --> 00:39:25,597
(BIRDS SQUAWKING)

641
00:39:45,850 --> 00:39:46,943
Hey.

642
00:39:50,021 --> 00:39:51,353
Thank you.

643
00:39:52,624 --> 00:39:55,526
Thank you. For letting
us leave that party early.

644
00:39:55,693 --> 00:39:59,130
Mmm. Of course. I
wanted to. I love this house.

645
00:39:59,297 --> 00:40:02,893
It's my father's refuge. Not
many people know about it.

646
00:40:04,569 --> 00:40:09,269
I know Gordon came to
the church, talked to you.

647
00:40:09,440 --> 00:40:11,170
It was just like you
said. (SCOFFS)

648
00:40:11,342 --> 00:40:13,811
He said you had the
virus. He was obsessed.

649
00:40:16,281 --> 00:40:17,408
And what did you say?

650
00:40:17,582 --> 00:40:20,416
That after the wedding we
would be leaving Gotham.

651
00:40:20,585 --> 00:40:22,076
And I would never see him again.

652
00:40:23,488 --> 00:40:24,922
Is that it?

653
00:40:25,089 --> 00:40:26,819
What are you asking me?

654
00:40:27,525 --> 00:40:28,891
I'm asking

655
00:40:29,727 --> 00:40:32,856
if there's any part of
you, however small,

656
00:40:33,031 --> 00:40:35,364
that still has feelings for him.

657
00:40:36,067 --> 00:40:39,834
And I swear I will
never ask you again.

658
00:40:42,106 --> 00:40:44,200
A part of me will
always care for him.

659
00:40:46,778 --> 00:40:48,440
But I married you.

660
00:40:49,113 --> 00:40:50,513
I love you.

661
00:40:57,855 --> 00:41:00,017
That's all I needed to know.

662
00:41:08,132 --> 00:41:09,910
- Where are they?
- GOON: <i>Don Falcone, he just...</i>

663
00:41:09,934 --> 00:41:11,493
Where are they?

664
00:41:13,271 --> 00:41:14,330
You don't give up, do you?

665
00:41:14,505 --> 00:41:16,440
Your son has
Alice Tetch's virus.

666
00:41:16,607 --> 00:41:20,237
He's killed two people we know
of. Every cop in this city is after him.

667
00:41:20,411 --> 00:41:21,435
Where is he?

668
00:41:29,354 --> 00:41:30,447
You knew?

669
00:41:30,621 --> 00:41:33,853
That Mario had the
same virus as Barnes? No.

670
00:41:34,025 --> 00:41:36,051
I knew he was in danger,
but I didn't know why.

671
00:41:37,161 --> 00:41:38,595
I never suspected this.

672
00:41:38,763 --> 00:41:42,222
You're saying the attacks
on Mario, the car bomb...

673
00:41:42,400 --> 00:41:43,766
It's because of the virus?

674
00:41:43,935 --> 00:41:46,404
How is that possible?
Who knew he had it?

675
00:41:46,571 --> 00:41:47,664
I can't tell you that.

676
00:41:50,742 --> 00:41:52,802
I'll send my men
to bring Mario in.

677
00:41:54,078 --> 00:41:56,377
You think I'd trust Lee's
life with these two goons?

678
00:41:57,015 --> 00:41:58,745
<i>Tell me where they are.</i>

679
00:41:58,916 --> 00:42:01,351
If I do that, you'll kill
him. I know you, James.

680
00:42:02,820 --> 00:42:04,288
Mario is my son.

681
00:42:04,889 --> 00:42:08,223
There is nothing and no
one more valuable to me.

682
00:42:08,393 --> 00:42:11,022
And if he does have this
sickness, he needs help.

683
00:42:11,195 --> 00:42:13,960
And if he kills Lee, he'll cross a
line he'll never come back from.

684
00:42:14,499 --> 00:42:18,163
<i>Even if he's cured,
knowing that will destroy him.</i>

685
00:42:18,336 --> 00:42:19,861
I'm your only hope.

686
00:42:21,873 --> 00:42:23,774
Still, I'll send my men.

687
00:42:23,941 --> 00:42:25,671
You mean these two?

688
00:42:25,943 --> 00:42:27,138
(BOTH GROAN)

689
00:42:29,647 --> 00:42:30,945
Anyone else you want to send?

690
00:42:32,517 --> 00:42:34,418
Swear that you'll
bring him in alive.

691
00:42:34,585 --> 00:42:37,487
I swear. Now, where are they?

692
00:42:43,227 --> 00:42:45,822
MARIO: <i>She loves
him. She loves him.</i>

693
00:42:45,997 --> 00:42:47,693
<i>She loves him.</i>

694
00:42:47,865 --> 00:42:49,493
<i>She loves him.</i>

695
00:42:50,034 --> 00:42:51,866
<i>She loves him.</i>

696
00:42:52,036 --> 00:42:53,902
<i>She loves him.</i>

697
00:42:56,874 --> 00:42:58,103
(TIRES SCREECHING)

698
00:42:59,844 --> 00:43:01,813
<i>She loves him. She loves him.</i>

699
00:43:06,384 --> 00:43:07,384
Lee!

700
00:43:07,552 --> 00:43:08,576
DR. THOMPKINS: <i>Jim?</i>

701
00:43:29,907 --> 00:43:31,899
(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)

702
00:44:05,076 --> 00:44:06,076
English -SDH
